From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: apple_tristar_charger: Run the poll on an
 unbound queue

The charger's own queue asked for neither WQ_PERCPU nor WQ_UNBOUND, so
every boot warned in alloc_workqueue(). The poll sleeps on I2C and the
HDQ gauge and keeps no per-CPU state: make the queue unbound.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
index 6e8e8368a..63168f8cb 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
@@ -1446,7 +1446,8 @@ static int tristar_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 	init_completion(&chg->adc_done);
-	chg->wq = devm_alloc_workqueue(dev, "tristar-charger", WQ_HIGHPRI | WQ_FREEZABLE, 1);
+	chg->wq = devm_alloc_workqueue(dev, "tristar-charger",
+				       WQ_UNBOUND | WQ_HIGHPRI | WQ_FREEZABLE, 1);
 	if (!chg->wq)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	INIT_DELAYED_WORK(&chg->poll_work, tristar_poll);
